From: crick Debian Backports <backports@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 04 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: locales: publish only the Russian locale

Upstream generates a .pak for every locale in |platform_pak_locales| (74 on
desktop), which Debian ships as chromium-l10n (~118 MB installed for 54
languages). This repository publishes a single Russian-only package, so the
list is narrowed to "ru".

There is no command-line way to do this: |platform_pak_locales| in
build/config/locales.gni is the one list that drives every locale .pak
declared in chrome/app/generated_resources.grd. Narrowing it removes the
other locales from generation altogether, so the build also gets faster,
not just the output smaller.

en-US is unaffected: it comes from generated_resources.grd directly and is
never on this list - it is copied separately from out/Release/locales by
debian/rules.

---
 build/config/locales.gni | 17 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

--- a/build/config/locales.gni
+++ b/build/config/locales.gni
@@ -191,6 +191,22 @@
   platform_pak_locales -= extended_locales
 }
 
+# Debian modification (crick backports): publish only the Russian locale.
+#
+# Upstream generates a .pak for every locale in |platform_pak_locales| (74 on
+# desktop). Debian packages them all as chromium-l10n (~118 MB installed).
+# This repository publishes a single Russian-only package instead, so the list
+# is cut down to "ru" here. Everything else in Chromium is unaffected: en-US
+# comes from generated_resources.grd directly and is not on this list.
+#
+# Why this file and not --locales on the ninja command line: there is no such
+# argument. |platform_pak_locales| is the single list that drives every locale
+# .pak in chrome/app/generated_resources.grd, so narrowing it removes the other
+# locales from generation entirely (faster build too, not just smaller output).
+if (is_linux) {
+  platform_pak_locales = [ "ru" ]
+}
+
 # The base list for all platforms except Android excludes the extended locales.
 # Add or subtract platform specific locales below.
 if (is_chromeos) {
